  "_comment": "Seed-level SPECS for `dotnet run --project Tools/LevelTool -- generate [--plays N]`. 40 levels, difficulty rising with hard milestones at 10/20/30/40 and a breather after each. Element first appearances: hidden items (R23) 4 · hidden boxes (R17) 7 · locked items (R24) 9 · rewarded-ad slots (R20, extraSlots) 12 · locked boxes (R18) 14 · locked slots (R22) 17 · bigger boxes (R21): M from 5, L from 8, XL from 32 (after level 40 the game replays from level 5, so M and L are in the early levels). conveyor: a shared layout in Assets/CapsChaos/Content/Configs/ConveyorConfig/<id>.json. feeders: bottles per conveyor feeder (right, left, middle), whole rows. greed: 1 = easy (trays match what is on the belt), 0 = tense. clustering: 1 = long blocks of one colour. extraSlots: locked slots that open for coins / an ad (0 before level 12). modifiers: how MANY hidden rows / hidden trays / locked rows / locked trays (lockTurns [min, max]) and which open slots are locked (slotLocks), sizedTrays / sizes [min, max] (bigger boxes merged from same-colour trays of one lane); the tool places them from the seed and proves the level solvable (replay, else solver search). targetWin: [min, max] random-play win rate (%, 200 plays, open slots only) the level must land in — the tool redraws modifier places, then reseeds, until it does.",
